    <h2>Advanced Glaucoma Diagnostic Technology</h2>
    <h3>Optical Coherence Tomography (OCT)</h3>
    <p>Our OCT machine provides cross-sectional images of the retinal nerve fibre layer (RNFL) and optic nerve head with micrometre-level precision. RNFL thinning is one of the earliest detectable signs of glaucoma — often visible on OCT before any visual field changes occur. For patients from Ludhiana, this means we can detect glaucoma at a stage when treatment can completely prevent vision loss.</p>
    <h3>Humphrey Visual Field Analyser (HVFA)</h3>
    <p>The Humphrey HVFA is the gold standard for monitoring functional visual field loss in glaucoma patients. It maps your entire visual field to detect subtle blind spots or areas of reduced sensitivity caused by glaucomatous optic nerve damage. Regular HVFA tests for patients from Ludhiana help us track disease progression and adjust treatment promptly.</p>
    <h3>Non-Contact Tonometry & Goldmann Applanation Tonometry</h3>
    <p>Accurate IOP (intraocular pressure) measurement is the cornerstone of glaucoma management. We use both non-contact air-puff tonometry for screening and Goldmann applanation tonometry (gold standard) for accurate measurement, ensuring no patient from Ludhiana is misdiagnosed due to inaccurate pressure readings.</p>
